# Formbricks Integration Guidelines

## When to Apply This Rule

Apply when:
- Implementing or modifying Formbricks survey embeds
- Adding enrollment questionnaires to courses or programs
- Displaying survey responses in the Applications tab
- Modifying registration flows that include surveys
- Debugging Formbricks API integration
- Configuring hidden fields or survey URLs

## Core Principles

### 1. Survey Type Requirements
- **Always use Link Surveys** (not App or Website surveys)
- Link surveys are embeddable via iframe
- App/Website surveys won't work in the registration modal

### 2. Hidden Fields
- **Required fields:** `eduhubUserId`, `eduhubCourseId`
- **Optional field:** `eduhubEnrollmentId` (not available during registration)
- **Use `eduhub*` prefix** to avoid conflicts with Formbricks internal variables
- Configure hidden fields in Formbricks survey settings before using

### 3. Survey URL Resolution
```typescript
// Program default can be overridden by course-specific URL
const effectiveSurveyUrl = 
  course.formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl || 
  course.Program?.defaultFormbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl || 
  null;
```

### 4. Auto-submission Pattern
- Registration auto-submits when survey is completed
- Listen for `formbricksSurveyCompleted` postMessage event
- Hide submit button when using Formbricks (auto-submit only)
- Maintain backward compatibility with motivation letter for courses without surveys

## Component Usage

### FormbricksSurveyEmbed

**When to use:**
- Embedding surveys in registration modals
- Displaying surveys in any dialog or page
- Need to track survey completion

**Required props:**
```typescript
<FormbricksSurveyEmbed
  surveyUrl={effectiveSurveyUrl}
  userId={userId}
  courseId={course.id}
  enrollmentId={enrollmentId} // Optional, omit during registration
  onComplete={handleCompletion}
  onError={handleError}
  className="h-full"
/>
```

**Key features:**
- Automatically appends hidden fields to URL
- Validates postMessage origin for security
- Shows loading spinner while survey loads
- Error handling with user-friendly messages

**Security considerations:**
```typescript
// ALWAYS validate message origin
const handleMessage = (event: MessageEvent) => {
  try {
    const surveyOrigin = new URL(surveyUrl).origin;
    if (event.origin !== surveyOrigin) return;
  } catch {
    // Fail-secure: reject if origin can't be verified
    return;
  }
  // Process message...
};
```

### FormbricksResponsesDisplay

**When to use:**
- Displaying survey responses in Applications tab
- Showing enrollment questionnaire answers
- Replacing motivation letter display

**Required props:**
```typescript
<FormbricksResponsesDisplay
  courseId={courseId}
  userId={userId}
  enrollmentId={enrollmentId}
  formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl={effectiveSurveyUrl}
/>
```

**Key features:**
- Fetches responses via `getFormbricksResponses` GraphQL action
- Shows loading/error/empty states
- Displays question headlines and answers
- Indicates incomplete responses with warning

## GraphQL Integration

### Query Pattern

```typescript
import { GET_FORMBRICKS_RESPONSES } from '../../../../queries/formbricks';

const { data, loading, error } = useRoleQuery<
  GetFormbricksResponses, 
  GetFormbricksResponsesVariables
>(GET_FORMBRICKS_RESPONSES, {
  variables: { 
    courseId, 
    userId, 
    enrollmentId, 
    formbricksSurveyUrl: effectiveSurveyUrl 
  },
  fetchPolicy: 'cache-first',
  skip: !effectiveSurveyUrl,
});
```

**Important:**
- Use `cache-first` for performance (responses don't change frequently)
- Skip query if no survey URL configured
- Handle all states: loading, error, success, empty

### Response Structure

```typescript
{
  getFormbricksResponses: {
    success: boolean
    error?: string
    responses: [{
      id: string
      createdAt: string
      finished: boolean
      answers: [{
        questionId: string
        headline: string
        answer: string
      }]
    }]
    survey: {
      id: string
      name: string
    }
  }
}
```

## Registration Modal Integration

### Detection Pattern

```typescript
// Determine if Formbricks should be used
const effectiveSurveyUrl = 
  course.formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl || 
  course.Program?.defaultFormbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl || 
  null;

const hasFormbricksSurvey = !!effectiveSurveyUrl;
const useFormbricks = hasFormbricksSurvey && config.requiresInput;
```

### Conditional Rendering

```typescript
{/* Show Formbricks survey OR traditional motivation letter */}
{useFormbricks ? (
  <div className="flex-1" style={{ minHeight: '500px' }}>
    <FormbricksSurveyEmbed
      surveyUrl={effectiveSurveyUrl}
      userId={userId}
      courseId={course.id}
      onComplete={handleFormbricksComplete}
      onError={setError}
    />
  </div>
) : config.requiresInput ? (
  <textarea
    value={motivationLetter}
    onChange={(e) => setMotivationLetter(e.target.value)}
    // ... traditional input props
  />
) : null}

{/* Hide submit button when using Formbricks */}
{!useFormbricks && (
  <DialogActions>
    {/* Submit button */}
  </DialogActions>
)}
```

### Auto-submission Handler

```typescript
const handleFormbricksComplete = useCallback(() => {
  setFormbricksSurveyCompleted(true);
  
  // Auto-submit registration with placeholder text
  onSubmit({
    motivationLetter: '[Formbricks Survey Completed]',
    acceptTerms: true,
  }).then((result) => {
    if (result.success) {
      closeModal();
    } else {
      setError(result.error || t('errors.registration_failed'));
    }
  });
}, [onSubmit, closeModal, t]);
```

## Error Handling

### User-Facing Errors

```typescript
// Embed errors
if (hasError) {
  return (
    <div className="flex items-center justify-center h-64 bg-red-50 rounded-md">
      <p className="text-red-600">{t('course.formbricks.embed_error')}</p>
    </div>
  );
}

// Response fetch errors
if (error || !data?.getFormbricksResponses?.success) {
  return (
    <div className="text-sm text-red-500">
      {t('manageCourse.formbricks.error_loading_responses')}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Backend Errors

**Common errors and solutions:**

1. **"You can't use this method with this API key"**
   - API key lacks project/environment access
   - Solution: Edit API key in Formbricks, add project access

2. **"Invalid Formbricks survey URL format"**
   - Survey URL malformed or incorrect
   - Solution: Use Link Survey URL format

3. **"Formbricks API key missing"**
   - `FORMBRICKS_API_KEY` not set
   - Solution: Add to `.env` file, restart containers

