## Example Implementation

### Adding Survey to New Registration Type

```typescript
// 1. Check for survey configuration
const effectiveSurveyUrl = 
  course.formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl || 
  course.Program?.defaultFormbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl;

const useFormbricks = !!effectiveSurveyUrl && requiresInput;

// 2. Conditional rendering
{useFormbricks ? (
  <FormbricksSurveyEmbed
    surveyUrl={effectiveSurveyUrl}
    userId={userId}
    courseId={course.id}
    onComplete={handleFormbricksComplete}
    onError={setError}
  />
) : (
  <textarea /* traditional input */ />
)}

// 3. Auto-submit handler
const handleFormbricksComplete = useCallback(() => {
  onSubmit({
    motivationLetter: '[Formbricks Survey Completed]',
    acceptTerms: true,
  });
}, [onSubmit]);
```

### Displaying Responses in New View

```typescript
import { FormbricksResponsesDisplay } from 'path/to/component';

// In your component
const effectiveSurveyUrl = 
  enrollment.Course.formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl ||
  enrollment.Course.Program?.defaultFormbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl;

{effectiveSurveyUrl ? (
  <FormbricksResponsesDisplay
    courseId={enrollment.courseId}
    userId={enrollment.userId}
    enrollmentId={enrollment.id}
    formbricksEnrollmentSurveyUrl={effectiveSurveyUrl}
  />
) : (
  <div>{enrollment.motivationLetter}</div>
)}
```

## Summary

The Formbricks integration replaces traditional motivation letters with structured surveys, providing:
- Better user experience with modern question types
- Easier data collection and analysis for course managers
- Program-wide defaults with course-level overrides
- Seamless integration with existing registration flows
- Comprehensive error handling and security measures

Always prefer Formbricks surveys over plain text inputs when collecting structured enrollment data.
